# Database: Always Use Drizzle ORM

All database interactions must go through Drizzle ORM. Never use raw SQL strings, direct `pg` client queries, or any other ORM.

## Schema

Tables are defined in [src/db/schema.ts](mdc:src/db/schema.ts):

- `decks` — belongs to a `clerkUserId`, has `name`, `description`, timestamps
- `cards` — belongs to a `deckId` (cascades on delete), has `front`, `back`, timestamps

The db client is exported from [src/db/index.ts](mdc:src/db/index.ts).

## Query Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — use drizzle query builder
import { db } from '@/db';
import { decks, cards } from '@/db/schema';
import { eq } from 'drizzle-orm';

const userDecks = await db.select().from(decks).where(eq(decks.clerkUserId, userId));

await db.insert(cards).values({ deckId, front, back });

await db.update(decks).set({ name }).where(eq(decks.id, deckId));

await db.delete(cards).where(eq(cards.id, cardId));
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — never use raw SQL or other clients
import { sql } from 'pg';
const result = await sql`SELECT * FROM decks WHERE clerk_user_id = ${userId}`;
```

## Rules

- Import table references only from `@/db/schema`
- Import the db client only from `@/db`
- Use `drizzle-orm` helpers (`eq`, `and`, `or`, `inArray`, etc.) for conditions
- Never bypass Drizzle with raw queries or a separate database client
